{
  "dom_id": "step-q25767",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $5x-1>7$ or $2\\le 2x+5<16.$",
  "worked_solution": "We start by solving $5x-1>7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-1 & >7 \\\\ 5x & >8 \\\\ x & >\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237546/assets/0efcf15a3abee964ad2dfc0c1dac12a0f2f43c86180d2ead869fc2ee7b8e9c76.png)\n\nThen, we solve $2\\le 2x+5<16:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & \\le 2x+5<16 \\\\ 2-5 & \\le 2x<16-5 \\\\ -3 & \\le 2x<11 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & \\le x<\\frac{11}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237546/assets/22f51dad4248c565cd3afcf03ec9f5a8c50494ad79ed1366b3513083be27182a.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237546/assets/e769eea6e55f7138cbce08cb285253fc1c710c2e39384994a8b36bd43a41ea32.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\ge -\\frac{3}{2}.$  We can write this using interval notation as $[-\\frac{3}{2},\\infty ).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
